================================================================================
WORK ORDERS CREATED FOR EVERYTHING STILL OPEN (306-314)
================================================================================
Each carries today's verified context + acceptance criteria, so any session (or
person) can pick it up cold.

  306  Media-layer audio routing (unroute own ch / route to other ch)
       - AWAITING YOUR GO: it changes the look model. Spec is written.
  307  SRT passphrase via project credentials (encrypted SRT, no plaintext secret)
  308  Split "operator monitor" from "confine pointer" (the welded setting that
       caged your mouse) - built behind operatorTools.pointerConfine when you say
  309  Async device-view probes - the REAL fix for xrandr blocking the whole
       server (~160ms per cache miss, measured); 4ab0c2d only bounded the hang
  310  One unit on the volume wire - kill the dB/linear double-send seen in the
       caspar log (last-write-wins hides it today)
  311  Autosave must not RESURRECT a factory-reset-trashed project (5d01bca
       protected the contents; the empty-shell recreation remains)
  312  Reassert audio-only routes after a Caspar restart - your route matrix is
       config now, but the routes themselves die with Caspar and only the
       browser recreates them
  313  rAF-throttle the cable-overlay resize handler (small; flagged, unmeasured)
  314  Laptop NVIDIA PRIME env for casparcg-server.service - BLOCKED on secure
       boot being disabled first; conditional drop-in so the tower is unaffected

Priority suggestion for the release: 312 and 311 are correctness holes an
operator will hit; 310 and 309 are hygiene; 306/307/308 are features on your
word; 313 is a nicety; 314 is hardware-gated.


